=== Phase 15 W4: UEFI product media — STRUCTURAL GATES PASS, QEMU-UNVERIFIED ===

Run: 2026-08-18 (this commit)
Host: CachyOS Linux, QEMU 11.0.3, edk2-ovmf 202605-1
Vendored Genode: 26.05 (commit 492a510242)
Vendored GRUB2 EFI binary: genode/contrib/grub2-eb7172dee270fbd9f1bc862d46725fd1fb21d1ea/boot/grub2/grub2_64.efi
Pinned OVMF: var/ovmf/OVMF_CODE.fd (2024.02, pre-W^X-regression)
Bender: STOCK (no NOP patch; per the W1 OUTCOME, the reverted NOP must NOT be re-applied)

=== STATUS (W4 acceptance) ===

W4 acceptance is HOST-SIDE STRUCTURAL VERIFICATION plus honest boot-gap
recording (D15.16, 2026-08-18 pivot). Per the W1 evidence, the QEMU
UEFI boot of the UEFI media is EXPECTED to fail (vendored GRUB2 EFI +
bender check_mem NOP gap); the scenario's real acceptance metric is
the structural gates (sgdisk -p / mdir / e2ls). Real-hardware UEFI
boot on the 17ZD90N-VX7BK is the 15-3 deliverable.

Both UEFI scenarios (SATA and NVMe envelopes) achieved 3/3
structural gates PASS plus the honest gap message. The end-to-end
dist wiring produced a structurally-correct UEFI .img in var/dist/
for the 15-3 real-hardware flashing run.

