=== UEFI partition layout (D15.13, binding W4 contract) ===

  P1   ESP     FAT32  typecode=EF00  label=ESP          64 MiB
                 /EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI  (grub2_64.efi renamed)
                 /boot/grub/grub.cfg
                 /boot/font.pf2
  P2   (ABSENT — intentional; see scenario header + §4.3.1)
  P3   GENODE  ext2  typecode=8300  label=GENODE       128 MiB
                 /boot/{bender,sel4,image.elf}  (bootloader modules)
                 /system/{bin,lib,init,themes,tars,pkg_*.xml,bake/}
  P4   SPONGE-DATA  ext2  typecode=8300  label=SPONGE-DATA  319 MiB
                 (added by tool/mkdata per docs/14 §4.3)

The P2-absent choice preserves `partition number="3"` for
part_block and tool/mkdata's `--new=4` grow sequence. Both work
UNCHANGED across BIOS and UEFI media — the same tool/mkdata
sequence, the same part_block pin, the same hybrid MBR semantics.

=== Run #1: UEFI SATA (sponge-desktop-disk-uefi.run) ===

Build command: make -j1 -C genode/build/x86_64 \
  run/sponge-desktop-disk-uefi KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc \
  SPONGE_BAKE_PROFILE=minimal
Log: var/logs/w4-uefi-sata-build.log

Structural gates (3/3 PASS):
  1. sgdisk -p on [run_dir].img:
     - P1=EF00(ESP, 64 MiB, sector 2048) — PASS
     - P3=8300(GENODE, 128 MiB, sector 133120) — PASS
     - P2 absent — PASS
  2. mdir on the .img's ESP (offset 1 MiB):
     - EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI (1,007,616 bytes) — PASS
     - /boot/grub/grub.cfg — PASS
     - /boot/font.pf2 — PASS
     - 16 files total in the FAT volume
  3. e2ls on the .img's P3 (extracted via dd skip=133120):
     - /system/bake: bake_manifest.json + config.defaults + theme.defaults
     - /system/bin: alpha_probe, boot_fb, calculatorform, decorator,
       hello, init, pdf_view, report_rom, sponge-de, sponge_configd,
       sponge_files, sponge_pkgd, sponge_themed, terminal, textedit,
       window_layouter, wm
     - /system: bake, bin, boot, config, default.theme, init, lib,
       light.theme, pkg_hello.xml, pkg_index.xml, pkg_terminal.xml,
       qt6_dejavusans.tar, qt6_libqgenode.tar

QEMU boot (≤180 s, expected to time out per D15.16):
  - OVMF BdsDxe loaded Boot0001 from the SATA disk
  - OVMF started Boot0001 (the GRUB2 EFI binary)
  - No further output (the vendored grub2_64.efi with stock bender
    hits the multiboot2 loader / W^X trap on this host's OVMF dated
    2026-05; the W1 evidence required a bender NOP to get past
    this stage, but per the W4 plan bender stays STOCK)
  - 180 s timeout fired; honest gap message printed; exit 0
  - QEMU log size: 529 bytes (just the OVMF handoff lines)

=== Run #2: UEFI NVMe envelope (sponge-desktop-disk-uefi-nvme.run) ===

Build command: make -j1 -C genode/build/x86_64 \
  run/sponge-desktop-disk-uefi-nvme KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc \
  SPONGE_BAKE_PROFILE=minimal
Log: var/logs/w4-uefi-nvme-build.log

Structural gates (3/3 PASS):
  1. sgdisk -p on the bootloader .img:
     - P1=EF00(ESP, 64 MiB) — PASS
     - P3=8300(GENODE, 32 MiB) — PASS (just the bootloader modules)
     - P2 absent — PASS
  2. mdir on the bootloader .img's ESP:
     - EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI (1,007,616 bytes) — PASS
     - /boot/grub/grub.cfg — PASS
     - /boot/font.pf2 — PASS
     - 16 files total
  3. e2ls on the NVMe disk's P3 (bin/nvme_disk.img extracted):
     - /system/bake: bake_manifest.json + config.defaults + theme.defaults
     - /system/bin: alpha_probe, calculatorform, decorator, hello, init,
       pdf_view, report_rom, sponge-de, sponge_configd, sponge_files,
       sponge_pkgd, sponge_themed, terminal, textedit, window_layouter, wm
     - /system: bake, bin, config, default.theme, init, lib, light.theme,
       pkg_hello.xml, pkg_index.xml, pkg_terminal.xml, qt6_dejavusans.tar,
       qt6_libqgenode.tar

QEMU boot (≤180 s, expected to time out per D15.16):
  - OVMF BdsDxe loaded Boot0001 (the .img's GRUB2 EFI)
  - OVMF started Boot0001
  - GRUB2 EFI loaded bender
  - bender printed "Bender Version 0.9-beta7-51-g28ba2ad-dirty"
  - bender printed "Bender: Hello World."
  - bender rejected type=4 (EfiBootServicesData) region overlap:
    "Reserved memory 800000+8000 type=4 overlaps with phdr 20835f+609901"
  - bender exited with status 2; system rebooted (3x retry loops,
    each 180 s; total 540 s observed)
  - 180 s timeout fired per retry; honest gap message printed; exit 0
  - QEMU log size: 962 bytes (OVMF + GRUB2 + bender failure output)

This is the W1 OVMF W^X + bender NOP gap, REPRODUCED HONESTLY in
the W4 NVMe scenario (the NVMe scenario gets further because the
boot FAILED in a different place — the bender is the same STOCK
binary, but the NVMe scenario's multiboot2 path actually runs the
bender executable, which then fails on the type=4 region overlap).
The SATA scenario's bender failure happens earlier (inside the
GRUB2 EFI binary's multiboot2 loader, before bender even runs).

