=== Run #5: BIOS regression (./tool/dist --help / --print-only) ===

  mojo tool/dist.mojo --print-only
    → make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-desktop-disk ... + .iso
    → firmware selector: bios (default unchanged)
    → target stage: var/dist/...{img,iso} (both .img and .iso)
  mojo tool/dist.mojo --print-only --storage nvme
    → make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-desktop-disk-nvme ... + .iso
    → firmware selector: bios (default unchanged)
    → target stage: var/dist/...{img,iso} (both .img and .iso)

BIOS path is regression-free. The W4 changes are strictly additive
on the UEFI branch.

=== Honest disclaimers (W4) ===

  * The QEMU UEFI boot does NOT pass. Per D15.16 and the W1 evidence,
    the UEFI QEMU cell stays a documented gap. The honest gap message
    in the W4 scenarios' exit output is the W4 acceptance signal —
    host-side structural gates PASS + the QEMU boot fails (no "Genode
    v..." banner, the bender multiboot2 path fails as expected).
  * bender stays STOCK. The W1 reverted-NOP is NOT re-applied.
    The 15-3 protocol records the bender-rebuild fallback if the
    real 17ZD90N-VX7BK also fails to load.
  * QGenodeScreen 1×1 race (D14.8(b)) on boot_fb: cannot be evaluated
    under OVMF (the bender/GRUB2 stage hangs first). Recorded as
    blocked-by-W1 in docs/evidence/phase15-index.md §8 entry.
    Deferred to 15-3 real-hardware observation. NOT faked.
  * No vendored-tree edits (bender md5 = c2018704ccc53202591e64246631e925,
    the stock binary; no NOP). boot_fb is in-tree
    (genode/repos/os/src/driver/framebuffer/boot/, license GPLv2 with
    linking exception per the vendored tree's COPYING).
  * No commits to git (per the goal); no `sudo` (AGENTS.md §5.5);
    no concurrent makes in genode/build/x86_64 (Phase 12 row-28
    discipline).
  * P2 absent is the BINDING W4 partition-number contract. It is
    NOT an oversight or a bug; the alternatives (P1=BIOS-boot +
    P2=ESP + P3=GENODE; P1=ESP + P2=GENODE) would require either
    a vendored-tree edit or re-pinning part_block / redoing
    tool/mkdata for the UEFI path. The P2-absent choice preserves
    `partition number="3"` and tool/mkdata's P4 grow sequence
    unchanged across BIOS and UEFI.

